 "notes_for_editor": "Record says first lens order 5 in 1860 (USLHS); LighthouseFriends says first-order Fresnel in 1857 and a 3.5-order bivalve in 1903; unresolved, both stated in text. Keeper dwelling 1837 (LF) vs 1838 (USLHS). LighthouseFriends is a secondary, copyrighted source and carries several anecdotes (Scott family, 1925 Millers, cocoa pudding) with no primary check; consider verifying. No NRHP text digitised. Roster copied from USLHS place page; Charles E. Schumacher appears under both principal keeper and USCG; Ira Lewis 1957-59 overlaps. Putnam page labels (scan 62, 95) uncertain printed numbers. Lighthouse Board 1899 volume has unreliable page index; scan pages 24 and 116 from corpus.py page. Visit hours/tower climb not verified from the operator site (blocked). Bulletin 1939 quote is from garbled two-column OCR. Fact-check 2026-10-22: removed unsupported characteristic and first_lit; Johnson cited to scan page 167 (not index p.102). Cost figures differ: Star $30.7M project vs Almanack $44M overall effort. LighthouseFriends' 1898 oil-engine date differs from the Board's 1897 report. Nothing in the roster was matched by table column position.",
